url: "https://github.com/MichailSemoglou/tramage"
abstract: "A Python package for constrained-palette halftoning. Given a continuous-tone image and a small, designer-chosen palette, tramage redistributes the quantization error using the palette's own covariance geometry in Oklab: error is damped along the palette's degenerate directions and left alone where the palette can absorb it. The shaping matrix is closed-form and computed once per palette; dithering costs one 3x3 matrix multiplication per pixel beyond ordinary error diffusion. On a 124-image corpus (Kodak24 + CQ100), it reduces perceptual error (S-CIELAB dE) by a median of up to 21% at small-to-moderate palette sizes and matches or beats the matrix-valued Damera-Venkata prior art in that regime. The package includes the evaluation harness, corpus manifests, and analysis scripts needed to reproduce every reported number."
keywords:
  - error diffusion
  - color quantization
  - halftoning
  - palette design
